---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const post = {
  title: 'Security Best Practices for WhatsApp Web',
  date: 'December 28, 2025',
  readTime: '7 min read',
  category: 'Security',
  author: 'WhatsApp Web Team'
};
---

<Layout title={`${post.title} - WhatsApp Web Blog`}>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 py-24 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <!-- Header -->
    <header class="text-center">
      <div class="flex items-center justify-center gap-3">
        <span class="rounded-full bg-red-100 px-3 py-1 text-sm font-medium text-red-800">
          {post.category}
        </span>
        <span class="text-gray-500">{post.readTime}</span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="mt-6 text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-gray-900 md:text-5xl" data-testid="blog-post-title">
        {post.title}
      </h1>
      <div class="mt-6 flex items-center justify-center gap-4 text-gray-600">
        <span>By {post.author}</span>
        <span>•</span>
        <time>{post.date}</time>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- Featured Image -->
    <div class="mt-12 flex h-64 items-center justify-center rounded-2xl bg-gradient-to-r from-red-600 to-red-800 md:h-96">
      <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="h-32 w-32 text-white/60" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
        <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="1.5" d="M9 12l2 2 4-4m5.618-4.016A11.955 11.955 0 0112 2.944a11.955 11.955 0 01-8.618 3.04A12.02 12.02 0 003 9c0 5.591 3.824 10.29 9 11.622 5.176-1.332 9-6.03 9-11.622 0-1.042-.133-2.052-.382-3.016z" />
      </svg>
    </div>

    <!-- Content -->
    <div class="prose prose-lg mx-auto mt-12 max-w-3xl" data-testid="blog-post-content">
      <p class="lead text-xl text-gray-600">
        Security is paramount when handling business communications. This guide covers essential security practices to protect your WhatsApp Web account and customer data.
      </p>

      <div class="rounded-lg bg-red-50 border border-red-200 p-6 not-prose my-8">
        <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
          <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="h-6 w-6 text-red-600 flex-shrink-0" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M12 9v2m0 4h.01m-6.938 4h13.856c1.54 0 2.502-1.667 1.732-3L13.732 4c-.77-1.333-2.694-1.333-3.464 0L3.34 16c-.77 1.333.192 3 1.732 3z" />
          </svg>
          <div>
            <h4 class="font-semibold text-red-800">Important Security Notice</h4>
            <p class="mt-1 text-red-700">Always keep your WhatsApp session secure. Unauthorized access to your account can compromise customer data and business communications.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2>Account Security</h2>

      <h3>Strong Password Practices</h3>
      <p>
        Your WhatsApp Web account password is your first line of defense. Follow these guidelines:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Use a unique password not shared with other services</li>
        <li>Include a mix of uppercase, lowercase, numbers, and symbols</li>
        <li>Minimum 12 characters recommended</li>
        <li>Never share your password with anyone</li>
        <li>Change passwords immediately if compromise is suspected</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Session Management</h3>
      <p>
        WhatsApp Web uses device-based sessions. Manage them carefully:
      </p>

      <div class="rounded-lg bg-gray-50 p-6 not-prose my-8">
        <h4 class="font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-4">Session Security Tips</h4>
        <ul class="space-y-3">
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="h-5 w-5 text-green-600 flex-shrink-0 mt-0.5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7" />
            </svg>
            <span class="text-gray-600">Regularly review active sessions in Settings</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="h-5 w-5 text-green-600 flex-shrink-0 mt-0.5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7" />
            </svg>
            <span class="text-gray-600">Remove any unrecognized devices immediately</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="h-5 w-5 text-green-600 flex-shrink-0 mt-0.5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7" />
            </svg>
            <span class="text-gray-600">Use "Log out all devices" if you suspect a breach</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="h-5 w-5 text-green-600 flex-shrink-0 mt-0.5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7" />
            </svg>
            <span class="text-gray-600">Log out when using shared or public computers</span>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <h2>Data Protection</h2>

      <h3>Multi-Tenant Isolation</h3>
      <p>
        WhatsApp Web uses schema-per-tenant database isolation. Each company's data is stored in a separate database schema, ensuring complete data separation:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>No cross-tenant data access possible</li>
        <li>Each tenant has its own encryption keys</li>
        <li>Data is isolated at the database level</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Encryption</h3>
      <p>
        Your data is protected with encryption at rest and in transit:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>In Transit:</strong> All API calls use HTTPS/TLS encryption</li>
        <li><strong>At Rest:</strong> Sensitive data is encrypted in the database</li>
        <li><strong>WhatsApp Messages:</strong> End-to-end encrypted by WhatsApp</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Team Security</h2>

      <h3>Role-Based Access Control</h3>
      <p>
        Use the permission system to limit access based on job requirements:
      </p>

      <div class="rounded-lg bg-gray-50 p-6 not-prose my-8">
        <h4 class="font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-4">Permission Best Practices</h4>
        <div class="space-y-4">
          <div>
            <h5 class="font-medium text-gray-900">Principle of Least Privilege</h5>
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">Only grant permissions that are necessary for the role. Members don't need admin access if they're only handling customer chats.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h5 class="font-medium text-gray-900">Regular Permission Audits</h5>
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">Review team permissions quarterly. Remove access for departed employees immediately.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h5 class="font-medium text-gray-900">Export Permission Control</h5>
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">Limit export capabilities to trusted team members to prevent data leakage.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h3>Audit Logging</h3>
      <p>
        All actions are logged for security and compliance. Use the audit log to:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Track who accessed what data</li>
        <li>Monitor message sending activity</li>
        <li>Detect unusual behavior patterns</li>
        <li>Investigate security incidents</li>
        <li>Meet compliance requirements</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>WhatsApp-Specific Security</h2>

      <h3>QR Code Safety</h3>
      <p>
        When scanning the QR code to connect WhatsApp:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Only scan codes from trusted WhatsApp Web sessions</li>
        <li>Never share screenshots of QR codes</li>
        <li>QR codes expire after 30 seconds for security</li>
        <li>If you didn't initiate the connection, don't scan</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Ban Prevention</h3>
      <p>
        Avoid actions that might trigger WhatsApp's anti-abuse systems:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Don't send bulk messages to unknown contacts</li>
        <li>Avoid sending the same message repeatedly</li>
        <li>Respect message rate limits</li>
        <li>Don't use the platform for spam or unsolicited marketing</li>
      </ul>

      <div class="rounded-lg bg-yellow-50 border border-yellow-200 p-6 not-prose my-8">
        <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
          <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="h-6 w-6 text-yellow-600 flex-shrink-0" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M13 16h-1v-4h-1m1-4h.01M21 12a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z" />
          </svg>
          <div>
            <h4 class="font-semibold text-yellow-800">If You Get Banned</h4>
            <p class="mt-1 text-yellow-700">WhatsApp Web will detect ban status and display guidance. Your message history is preserved locally, but you won't be able to send or receive until the ban is lifted.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2>Physical Security</h2>
      <p>
        Don't forget physical security measures:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Lock your computer when leaving your desk</li>
        <li>Use screen privacy filters in public spaces</li>
        <li>Ensure your phone (for QR scanning) has a secure lock</li>
        <li>Be aware of shoulder surfing in open offices</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Incident Response</h2>
      <p>
        If you suspect a security breach:
      </p>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Log out all sessions</strong> - Use the "Log out all devices" feature immediately</li>
        <li><strong>Change your password</strong> - Create a new, strong password</li>
        <li><strong>Review audit logs</strong> - Check for unauthorized access</li>
        <li><strong>Contact support</strong> - Report the incident to our security team</li>
        <li><strong>Notify affected parties</strong> - If customer data was exposed, follow notification procedures</li>
      </ol>

      <h2>Security Checklist</h2>
      <div class="rounded-lg bg-gray-50 p-6 not-prose my-8">
        <h4 class="font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-4">Weekly Security Review</h4>
        <div class="space-y-2">
          <label class="flex items-center gap-3">
            <input type="checkbox" class="h-4 w-4 rounded border-gray-300" />
            <span class="text-gray-600">Review active sessions</span>
          </label>
          <label class="flex items-center gap-3">
            <input type="checkbox" class="h-4 w-4 rounded border-gray-300" />
            <span class="text-gray-600">Check team permissions</span>
          </label>
          <label class="flex items-center gap-3">
            <input type="checkbox" class="h-4 w-4 rounded border-gray-300" />
            <span class="text-gray-600">Review audit logs for anomalies</span>
          </label>
          <label class="flex items-center gap-3">
            <input type="checkbox" class="h-4 w-4 rounded border-gray-300" />
            <span class="text-gray-600">Verify WhatsApp connection status</span>
          </label>
          <label class="flex items-center gap-3">
            <input type="checkbox" class="h-4 w-4 rounded border-gray-300" />
            <span class="text-gray-600">Remove departed team members</span>
          </label>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2>Conclusion</h2>
      <p>
        Security is an ongoing process, not a one-time setup. By following these best practices and maintaining vigilance, you can protect your business communications and customer data on WhatsApp Web.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Author Bio -->
    <div class="mt-16 border-t border-gray-200 pt-8">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-4">
        <div class="flex h-16 w-16 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-red-100">
          <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="h-8 w-8 text-red-600" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M16 7a4 4 0 11-8 0 4 4 0 018 0zM12 14a7 7 0 00-7 7h14a7 7 0 00-7-7z" />
          </svg>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="font-semibold text-gray-900">{post.author}</p>
          <p class="text-gray-600">Building the future of business communication.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Back to Blog -->
    <div class="mt-12 text-center">
      <a href="/blog" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-primary-600 hover:text-primary-700">
        <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="h-4 w-4" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M15 19l-7-7 7-7" />
        </svg>
        Back to Blog
      </a>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
